Market Challenges
EUV photoresist development involves complex material engineering and demanding process-integration requirements. Manufacturers must maintain consistent exposure sensitivity, resolution, and pattern quality while controlling defects during wafer processing. Variations in exposure dose and post-exposure baking conditions can affect critical dimensions and manufacturing yields.

Market Restraints
The high cost of specialized chemicals, research, and manufacturing infrastructure can restrict broader adoption. Photoresist suppliers must also meet stringent qualification requirements before their products can be integrated into semiconductor fabrication lines. Supply-chain dependencies and geopolitical uncertainties may further affect the availability and cost of essential materials.

